  "scope": "Same original residual representation: original split-torus detecting primes with exact unramified trace-zero adjoint H1 dimension equal to the symmetric degree, and bounded jointly detecting families with that dimension at every selected prime. The explicit small-image alternative and every earlier original arithmetic, symmetric and cohomological conclusion are retained.",
  "sourceAssemblyReview": "The actual finite linear subfield lower bound contains the canonical prime-field SL2. Its regular torus has order p-1 and eigenvalues already in the original residue field. Native distinct-eigenvector independence and basis construction produce the original diagonalizer without a general scalar-extension theorem for H1 or invariant kernels. The original root-fixing cocycle and native conjugate Chebotarev preserve one actual finite factor and local Frobenius. Native cyclic-image generation, symmetric trace invariants and the proved original-field unramified H1 comparison give exact local dimension n. Original H1 finiteness and native finite detecting families then give the bounded family. All apply to the same actual original modular-form residual witness. Small-image exclusions, remaining local deformation conditions, automorphy and literal higher continuation remain open. Default proof limits, pins and all linters are unchanged."
